Verse 1:
[C7]Amazing [F]grace! how sweet [Bb]the [F]sound, [C7]That [F]saved a wretch like me!
[C7]Ionce was [F]lost, but now am found, Was [Bb]blind, but now Isee.

Verse 2:
[C7]'Twas [F]grace that [Bb]taught [F]my heart to fear,
[C7]and [F]grace my fears relieved;
[C7]how [F]precious did that [Bb]grace appear
[C7]the [F]hour I first [Bb]believed.

Verse 3:
[C7]The [F]Lord has [Bb]promised [F]good to me,
[C7]his [F]word my [Bb]hope [C7]secures;
[C7]he [F]will my shield and [Bb]portion be,
[C7]as [F]long as life endures.

Verse 4:
[C7]Through [F]many dangers, toils, and snares,
[C7]I [F]have already come;
[C7]'tis [F]grace hath brought me [Bb]safe thus far,
[C7]and [F]grace will lead [Bb]me home.

Verse 5:
[C7]When [F]we've been [Bb]there [F]ten thousand years,
[C7]bright [F]shining as the sun,
[C7]we've [F]no less days to [Bb]sing God's praise
[C7]than [F]when we first [Bb]begun.
